{"type":"text","text":"## Found: Mario's horizontal position in the level — a 16-bit pair\n\n| Address | Role | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`$006D`** | page (high) byte | binary; counts how many 256-pixel pages Mario has travelled |\n| **`$0086`** | position within the page (low) byte | binary, 0–255 |\n\n**Absolute level x = `$006D` × 256 + `$0086`.** They are separate object-arrays (`$006D,X` / `$0086,X`); Mario is object slot 0. In World 1-1 the start reads `$006D`=0, `$0086`=40 (level x 40), with the camera (`$071C`/`$073F`) at 0.\n\n### How they were found\n- **Differential search (no reference):** snapshot at the 1-1 start (`$0086`=40), hold Right 40 frames, diff `increased` → 50 survivors including `$0086` (40→99). A second run showed `$0086` climbing 99→117 smoothly with Mario's motion.\n- **The page byte from the movement code:** `trace_writes` on `$0086` while standing still gave writer PC `$BF40`. Disassembly at `$BF3C–$BF46` is a 16-bit add: `lda $86,X / adc $00 / sta $86,X ; lda $6d,X / adc $02 / sta $6d,X` — the carry propagates from `$0086` into `$006D`, so `$006D` is the high byte.\n- **Natural wrap:** holding Right 360 frames from the start, `$0086` ran 40…253 then wrapped to 0, 6, 15, 24, 33, 41, and `$006D` changed **0→1 on exactly the frame `$0086` wrapped** (watch frames 156–162), while Mario stayed at on-screen x≈112 and the camera kept scrolling 0→185.\n\n### Write proofs\n- **`$0086`:** Paused at the 1-1 start (`$006D`=0, `$0086`=40, camera 0), wrote `$0086`=200 and stepped 2 frames. `list_sprites` showed Mario's OAM entries move from x=40/48 to **x=200/208**, and the screenshot showed the small Mario standing at the **right-hand bush** instead of on the left hill at x≈40.\n- **`$006D`:** From a live mid-level state (`$006D`=1, `$0086`=9, camera `$071C`=153, Mario on screen at x=112 = level 265), I wrote **only `$0086`=0**. `$006D` stayed 1 and Mario's OAM appeared at **x=103 = 256−153**, i.e. level 256. If the page byte were ignored, `$0086`=0 would be level 0 — 153 px *behind* the camera and off-screen; instead the screenshot showed Mario at the left of the hill with the Goomba to his right. That fixes `$006D` as the +256 page byte.\n\nBoth are recorded with `record_mapping` (source \"differential search\") and were promoted to the shared mapping file (now 12 addresses). The emulator is left running at the start of 1-1, with the live RAM writes rolled back via the save state."}
